claim.claim-text:
A portable briefcase-deployed flight and physical-assist exosuit system (2700), comprising:
      a rigid briefcase enclosure (2702) housing a collapsible multi-degree-of-freedom exoskeleton frame (2704) interconnected by shape-memory alloy deployment hinges (2706) configured to deploy into a wearable sealed exosuit lined with a viscoelastic zero-bounce kinetic-and-directed-energy-harvesting armor layer;
      at least one dorsal closed-loop thermodynamic power core (2708) utilizing 90 degrees Celsius graphene-coated hydrodynamic cavitation and 33.6 kV zero-voltage-switching nanosecond pulsed plasma to convert metabolic and actuator waste heat against ambient slipstream air into continuous electrical power and distilled water;
      a plurality of hybrid magnetoplasma and electrohydrodynamic ion thrusters (2712) powered by said power core (2708) and a supercapacitor buffer (2710) to generate vertical and vectorable flight thrust without liquid chemical propellants; and
      an air-gapped neural-command helmet (2716) comprising a non-invasive EEG and fNIRS brain-computer interface (2718) physically isolated from radio-frequency transceivers within a Mu-Metal Faraday shield (2720) and coupled exclusively through a unidirectional optical diode (2722) and post-quantum cryptographic enclave (2724) to prevent external takeover.

A load-bearing neural-controlled multi-tentacle exoskeleton system (2800), comprising:
      a dorsal chassis (2802) supporting four hyper-redundant continuum manipulator tentacles (2804), each having 9 degrees of freedom and terminating in a multi-fingered omni-claw (2806);
      bilateral 12-DOF load-bearing exoskeleton legs (2810) structurally coupled to said dorsal chassis (2802) through a sacral pelvic yoke (2808) and terminating in ground-contact force plates (2814), wherein said exoskeleton legs (2810) route combined chassis and tentacle payload forces directly to the ground to maintain less than 2.5 kg perceived load on a human operator spine;
      dual closed-loop thermodynamic power cores (2816) mounted in said dorsal chassis (2802) configured to harvest quasi-direct-drive actuator waste heat (2812) via 90 degrees Celsius cavitation and 33.6 kV nanosecond plasma to generate continuous electrical power and distilled water; and
      a wearable air-gapped neural-command cap (2818) devoid of wireless radio-frequency transceivers and coupled via a shielded optical link to translate operator brain intent into coordinated multi-tentacle and bipedal leg trajectories.
